              "id": "18069892"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Deletion of the gene leads to a strong decrease in intracellular growth in human monocytes (PubMed:10361301, PubMed:11115108). Mutant is unable to evade phagosome lysosome fusion, but retains the pore-forming activity (PubMed:10361301, PubMed:11115108). Mutation severely impairs the translocation into host cells of multiple effector proteins, including SidA, SidB, SidC, SidD, SidE, SidG, SidH, WipA and WipB (PubMed:15661013, PubMed:18069892). Loss of this gene has an effect on the levels of IcmS (PubMed:17040490)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"
